is a paper by Yasha Sol Dixin at all.

00:48:25.422 --> 00:48:26.562
So they made the connection.

00:48:28.942 --> 00:48:31.001
And so what happens is you have a system that

00:48:31.322 --> 00:48:33.402
follows the laws of physics. In particular, it

00:48:33.402 --> 00:48:34.942
follows the second law of thermodynamics.

00:48:35.642 --> 00:48:36.792
You start with structure,

00:48:37.682 --> 00:48:40.041
and you let it age like

00:48:40.042 --> 00:48:42.402
we all age. Right? And then in the end,

00:48:42.582 --> 00:48:44.762
it turns into noise. Like we

00:48:45.002 --> 00:48:46.862
turn into dust at one day, unfortunately.

00:48:47.682 --> 00:48:49.921
And then you study that process and you try

00:48:49.922 --> 00:48:52.194
to invert it. You say, okay, every

00:48:52.282 --> 00:48:54.302
little step let me create a

00:48:54.302 --> 00:48:56.322
force and do some work to move

00:48:56.322 --> 00:48:58.552
in the other direction. Right? So this one goes

00:48:59.031 --> 00:49:00.572
against the second law of thermodynamics,

00:49:01.092 --> 00:49:03.231
It is like an egg that you

00:49:03.232 --> 00:49:05.322
you turn into an omelette, This is

00:49:05.322 --> 00:49:07.481
like the omelette that turns into an egg. You don't

00:49:07.481 --> 00:49:09.361
actually see this happen in the real world,

00:49:09.842 --> 00:49:12.081
but you know, you could engineer it to happen if you're

00:49:12.082 --> 00:49:12.792
smart enough.

00:49:14.542 --> 00:49:16.702
And so we set out to use this

00:49:16.702 --> 00:49:18.222
theory to actually

00:49:19.822 --> 00:49:21.881
for something useful which is compute

00:49:21.882 --> 00:49:24.021
the free energy difference

00:49:24.021 --> 00:49:26.072
between let's say, a drug like molecule

00:49:26.512 --> 00:49:28.212
that is unbounds to a protein

00:49:28.842 --> 00:49:31.002
and a drug like molecule which is bound to

00:49:31.002 --> 00:49:33.122
a protein. You need that

00:49:33.122 --> 00:49:34.572
because you wanna figure out how

00:49:35.132 --> 00:49:36.722
how well does that molecule

00:49:37.442 --> 00:49:39.791
like to sit in a particular pocket

00:49:39.791 --> 00:49:41.802
of the protein. But it's actually

00:49:41.802 --> 00:49:43.861
very difficult calculation to do. And

00:49:43.862 --> 00:49:46.181
so what you need to do, if you just do MD simulation

00:49:46.181 --> 00:49:47.961
and you wait, you will wait forever.

00:49:48.392 --> 00:49:50.632
So you need to control it. So you need to apply a

00:49:50.632 --> 00:49:52.872
