00:51:06.717 --> 00:51:09.122
can get rid of that noise. And

00:51:09.262 --> 00:51:11.592
in fact, it's an optimal transport solution.

00:51:11.592 --> 00:51:13.932
So you need to solve the optimal transport problem

00:51:13.932 --> 00:51:16.354
between the initial distribution and the

00:51:16.442 --> 00:51:18.321
final distribution and those paths

00:51:18.721 --> 00:51:20.781
that that kind of control path you take

00:51:20.782 --> 00:51:23.021
is the optimal one. And it has zero

00:51:23.022 --> 00:51:25.242
variance if you do it right. That's amazing.

00:51:25.462 --> 00:51:26.042
Zero variance.

00:51:27.722 --> 00:51:29.882
And so we know how to do this. There's a paper

00:51:29.882 --> 00:51:31.782
called you know, optimal

00:51:32.002 --> 00:51:34.082
transport continuous normalizing flows by these guys

00:51:34.082 --> 00:51:36.291
here, Tom at all, where, you know, this

00:51:36.291 --> 00:51:38.472
